Embedded React: size a Text node by the lines it wraps into.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/layout/layout_engine.c,
engine/text/text_renderer.c, engine/text/text_renderer.h and
engine/tests/layout/test_layout.c. Proposed upstream as pull request #319.

The renderer breaks text at its node's width (unlimited lines by default, at
most numberOfLines), but layout gave an auto-height Text one line, or exactly
numberOfLines lines whether or not the text needed them. Wrapped text was cut
to its first line, and a short label with numberOfLines = 3 reserved three.
Layout now breaks the text the way the renderer does (er_text_wrap) at the
width the node gets and is as tall as the lines, capped by numberOfLines; a run
that fits on one line keeps its single-line measurement and costs nothing more.
The width a Text gets in a row is known only after flexing, so a row child
whose width flexed is measured again at that width, and a row's intrinsic
height distributes its free space by flexGrow and flexShrink before measuring
the children whose width changes. Measurements stay memoised per layout pass.

